  "title": "Digital Presence Foundation: LinkedIn Optimization + 30-Day Content Strategy",
  "content": "## Plan Overview\n\nThis plan has two parallel research tracks that feed into a final synthesis:\n\n1. **LinkedIn Profile Optimization** — Research current best practices and create a comprehensive profile optimization guide tailored to the user's B2B SaaS marketing positioning\n2. **Content Strategy Research** — Research high-performing content formats, posting cadences, and engagement tactics for both LinkedIn and Twitter/X in the marketing/tech niche\n3. **Competitor/Exemplar Analysis** — Study top B2B SaaS marketing voices to identify content patterns and gaps\n4. **Final Synthesis** — Combine all research into a complete deliverable: optimized profile recommendations + 30-day content calendar + templates + engagement playbook\n\nUncertainty is low (clear goal, clear audience, clear constraints), so we parallelize research and synthesize at the end with join='all'.",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "goal": "Research and compile LinkedIn profile optimization best practices for 2025-2026, specifically for B2B SaaS marketing professionals. Focus on: headline formulas with keywords (B2B, SaaS, content strategy, data-driven marketing), About section structure, Featured section strategy, Skills & endorsements for algorithm discoverability, banner image best practices, and Creator Mode optimization. Produce a detailed, actionable optimization checklist tailored to a Senior Marketing Manager positioning as an expert in 'practical, data-driven B2B content strategy and enablement'.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Research current high-performing content formats and posting best practices for LinkedIn and Twitter/X in 2025-2026 for B2B marketing thought leaders. Include: optimal posting frequency for each platform given 3-4 hrs/week constraint, best times to post, top-performing post formats (carousels, text posts, threads, polls, short video), character/length sweet spots, hashtag strategies, and algorithm-favored engagement patterns. Also research content repurposing strategies between LinkedIn and Twitter/X to maximize efficiency.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Identify and analyze 5-8 top-performing B2B SaaS marketing voices on LinkedIn and Twitter/X. Search for accounts like Chris Walker, Dave Gerhardt, Amanda Natividad, Lenny Rachitsky, or similar practitioners known for practical marketing insights. For each, analyze: content pillars they use, posting cadence, engagement levels, content formats that get the most traction, and how they balance educational vs. promotional content. Identify gaps and opportunities for someone positioning around 'practical, data-driven implementation' rather than theory.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Research trending topics and conversations in B2B SaaS marketing for early-to-mid 2026. Search for: current hot debates (AI in marketing, attribution challenges, content saturation, PLG vs sales-led), emerging tools and platforms, recent industry reports or data points that could be referenced in content, and seasonal marketing themes for the next 30 days. This will fuel specific content ideas for the calendar.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Synthesize all research into a comprehensive, polished deliverable with four sections:\n\n1. **LinkedIn Profile Optimization Guide** — Step-by-step checklist with specific copy suggestions for headline, About section, Featured section, skills, and banner based on Task 0 research. Include 2-3 headline options and a draft About section template.\n\n2. **30-Day Content Calendar** — A day-by-day calendar for LinkedIn (3-4 posts/week) and Twitter/X (5-7 posts/week) with specific content ideas organized into 4 content pillars (e.g., Data-Driven Tips, Tool/Tech Reviews, Implementation Playbooks, Industry Commentary). Each calendar entry should have: date, platform, content pillar, post format, topic/hook, and brief description. Ensure content can be produced within 3-4 hours/week.\n\n3. **Content Templates & Frameworks** — 5-6 reusable post templates (LinkedIn text post, LinkedIn carousel outline, Twitter/X thread structure, quick tip format, mini case study format, curated insight format) with fill-in-the-blank structures.\n\n4. **Engagement Playbook** — Daily/weekly engagement routine (15-20 min/day), key accounts to engage with, hashtag lists for each platform, and growth tactics for going from 750→1500 LinkedIn and 200→500 Twitter/X followers in 30 days.\n\nUse insights from Task 2 (exemplar analysis) to inform content angles and from Task 3 (trending topics) to fuel specific content ideas. Format everything in clean markdown.",
